window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["33"]={"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/burkina-faso":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"c51e683012ec7337c6d94862eb6e55cb884d6ef81ab0a62715cb2e65a6212371","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/burkina-faso","bytes":54955,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Burkina Faso travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-20T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-10-26T15:58:48+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Burkina Faso."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is due to the threat of terrorist attacks and terrorist kidnap, and the unstable political situation in the country."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/burkina-faso/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Limited consular support"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no British Embassy in Burkina Faso and all consular support is provided from the British Embassy in Accra, Ghana. They cannot provide in-person assistance."]},{"k":"p","s":["If there is serious violence, unrest or a deterioration in the security situation, it could be difficult to leave safely. Do not rely on the British government to evacuate you as they may not be able to do so. Have your own plans on how you would leave the country, make sure you keep all travel documentation up to date and monitor the local situation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel despite FCDO advice, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/burkina-faso/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK who choose to travel despite FCDO advice. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Burkina Faso’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Burkina Faso set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Embassy of Burkina Faso in Brussels","https://www.ambassadeduburkinafaso.be/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport must be valid for the duration of your stay and have 2 blank pages for entry stamps."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual Citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to enter Burkina Faso."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you live in the UK, ",["apply for a visa online or through the Embassy of Burkina Faso in Brussels","https://www.visaburkina.bf/en/home/"],". You cannot get a visa for Burkina Faso in the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are Burkinabe embassies in the West Africa region, including in Accra and Abidjan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To pass border control in Burkina Faso, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination, due to a risk of yellow fever transmission."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more details about health entry requirements and recommended vaccinations see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Burkina Faso guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/37/burkina-faso#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Burkina Faso"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are very likely to try to carry out attacks in Burkina Faso."]},{"k":"p","s":["Several terrorist groups operate in Burkina Faso, including Jama’a Nusrat ul-Islam wa al-Muslimin (JNIM) and Islamic State."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat from terrorism throughout the country, including increasingly in the capital, Ouagadougou. Terrorist attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places frequented by foreign nationals, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["diplomatic premises"]},{"k":"li","s":["conference centres"]},{"k":"li","s":["tourist sites"]},{"k":"li","s":["sporting and cultural events including music festivals"]},{"k":"li","s":["shopping centres"]},{"k":"li","s":["major roads and transport hubs"]},{"k":"li","s":["religious sites and places of worship, particularly churches"]},{"k":"li","s":["national parks and nature reserves"]},{"k":"li","s":["foreign, national or local government buildings"]},{"k":"li","s":["large crowds"]},{"k":"p","s":["There may be a heightened risk of attack during festivals, and religious and public holiday periods. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of the local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent attacks across Burkina Faso, particularly close to the borders with Mali, Niger and Côte d’Ivoire and in the eastern region."]},{"k":"p","s":[["See also road safety","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/burkina-faso/safety-and-security"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Examples of significant attacks include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in August 2024, at least 400 people were killed in a village attack in Barsalogho, Sanmatenga"]},{"k":"li","s":["in July 2024, the office of Doctors Without Borders (MSF) was attacked by gunfire in Djibo, Sahel"]},{"k":"li","s":["in February 2024, at least 15 people were killed in an attack on a church in Essakane, Oudalan"]},{"k":"li","s":["in February 2024, at least 12 people were killed in an attack on a mosque in Natiaboani, Gourma"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2023, two foreign nationals were killed in an attack on a commercial truck convoy on the N3 (near Diori), Sahel"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2023, around 20 people were killed in attacks on 6 villages in the southwest of Seytenga including Foufou, Mira and Lipsi"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorist kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["There’s a very high threat of kidnapping by Al-Qaeda and regional Islamic State-affiliated groups in Burkina Faso. These include Jamaat Nusrat al-Islam wal Muslimeen (JNIM) and Islamic State Greater Sahara (ISGS ), who operate throughout Mali, Niger and Burkina Faso."]},{"k":"p","s":["A number of foreign nationals have been kidnapped and killed in Burkina Faso in recent years, especially in the northeast of the country."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals are seen as legitimate targets, including tourists, humanitarian aid workers, journalists and business travellers. If you are kidnapped, the reason for your presence is unlikely to protect you or secure your safe release."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re working or travelling in Burkina Faso, you should be aware of the risk of terrorist kidnapping. You should maintain a high level of vigilance at all times, including when travelling. You should be particularly vigilant when walking in crowded public places, including camps for displaced people, religious gatherings and insecure spaces like places of worship, markets, shopping malls, hotels, bars, night clubs, restaurants, nature reserves and national parks, and transport hubs. You should avoid regular patterns of travel and aim to only travel during daylight hours."]},{"k":"p","s":["The long-standing policy of the British government is to not make substantive concessions to hostage takers. The British government considers that paying ransoms and releasing prisoners builds the capability of terrorist groups and finances their activities. This can, in turn, increase the risk of further hostage-taking. The Terrorism Act (2000) makes payments to terrorists illegal."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["The political situation also remains unstable following the military coup on 30 September 2022. Further coups are possible. If you choose to travel to Burkina Faso, you should remain vigilant and monitor local media."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government has declared a state of emergency in the regions of:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Centre-Est"]},{"k":"li","s":["Est"]},{"k":"li","s":["Centre Nord"]},{"k":"li","s":["Nord"]},{"k":"li","s":["Boucle du Mouhoun"]},{"k":"li","s":["Sahel"]},{"k":"li","s":["Hauts-Bassins"]},{"k":"li","s":["Cascades"]},{"k":"p","s":["The measure gives security forces extra powers to conduct searches, restrict freedom of movement and detain persons of interest. Some civil rights may be suspended, including the right to protest and to hold large meetings. The military takeover in neighbouring Niger in 2023 may lead to unrest or protests in Ouagadougou."]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests are common in Burkina Faso. Avoid political rallies, gatherings and demonstrations. Crowds can gather quickly and may become violent. Foreign, national and local government facilities have been targeted and damaged in previous demonstrations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor the local news to help you avoid such gatherings. If you become aware of a crowd gathering, leave the area immediately."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vehicle crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is an increasing number of vehicle hold-ups on roads outside Ouagadougou. Drivers that refuse to stop when flagged down have been shot at."]},{"k":"p","s":["Armed groups have also stopped drivers to rob passengers and their vehicles. Criminals have stopped public buses to assault and rob passengers, particularly at night."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Street crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Street crime is a serious risk for foreign visitors. Most incidents are opportunist snatches of purses, wallets, jewellery and other valuables. Thieves are particularly active near the UN Circle and the former Central Market in Ouagadougou, and are often armed. Do not carry valuables in public places or walk alone at night."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Criminal kidnapping"]},{"k":"p","s":["Kidnapping by criminal groups is widespread across Niger, Mali and Burkina Faso. There is a possibility that criminal groups could sell people they kidnap as hostages to terrorist organisations."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals are seen as legitimate targets, including tourists, humanitarian aid workers, journalists and business travellers. If you are kidnapped, the reason for your presence is unlikely to protect you or secure your safe release. You should avoid regular patterns of travel and aim to only travel during daylight hours."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry your passport or residence permit."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. During this time, do not:"]},{"k":"li","s":["eat, drink, smoke or chew gum in public in the daytime, including in your car"]},{"k":"li","s":["play loud music or dance"]},{"k":"li","s":["swear in public"]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["The death penalty was reinstated in Burkina Faso in October 2026 for certain offences, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["acts of terrorism"]},{"k":"li","s":["espionage"]},{"k":"li","s":["treason"]},{"k":"li","s":["parricide"]},{"k":"li","s":["importing expired or banned products that cause death"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not get involved in drugs of any kind. If you’re convicted of possessing or distributing any illegal drug, you can expect heavy fines and long jail sentences. Local prison conditions are harsh."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras and filmmaking"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not take pictures of military or other government installations."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same sex sexual activity and the ‘promotion’ of same-sex relationships is a criminal offence in Burkina Faso. If convicted, such charges could lead to prison sentences of up to 5 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is little to no public acceptance of LGBT+ people or identities in Burkina Faso. There is an increased risk of harassment or violence against anyone thought to be part of the LGBT+ community, or perceived to be supporting their rights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict customs regulations about taking cultural objects like masks, religious materials and antiquities out of Burkina Faso. If you’re unsure about buying any souvenirs you find for sale, contact the Ministry of Culture."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["A few of the larger hotels and restaurants in Ouagadougou accept credit cards. You’re unlikely to be able to use them anywhere outside the capital. There are a few ATMs in Ouagadougou, but they only accept Visa cards."]},{"k":"p","s":["The best option is to bring US dollars in cash to exchange."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to drive in Burkina Faso, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Get security advice about travelling by road in Burkina Faso."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Burkina Faso. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["1949 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Roads, even if they are paved, are in a poor state of repair. Road conditions off the main roads are often difficult, especially in the rainy season from June to October. Vehicles are often in poor condition."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid travelling at night, even if using a local driver. Roads have very limited lighting, and vehicles often have no headlights. Livestock, pedestrians and motorbikes on the roads are additional hazards."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks on major roads and transport routes by terrorists are increasing, including through the use of landmines and other explosive devices. This is particularly the case in areas where terrorist groups are operational and near border areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is danger of armed attacks on all roads, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["from Ouagadougou to Bobo-Dioulasso"]},{"k":"li","s":["from Bobo-Dioulasso to Côte d’Ivoire"]},{"k":"li","s":["from Fada to Benin and Togo"]},{"k":"li","s":["to Benin, Bogandée and Gayeri"]},{"k":"li","s":["to Niger"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is limited access to phone networks, so consider taking a satellite phone in case you break down or have another emergency. Always carry drinking water with you."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["The rainy season normally runs from June to October. Torrential rains can cause floods and landslides. Monitor local weather reports and expect difficulties when travelling to affected areas during this season."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 18 from Ouagadougou and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Outside Ouagadougou, call the universal emergency number 112."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you get no response, you will need to get local advice about the closest hospital and how to get to it."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Burkina Faso","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/37/burkina-faso#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Burkina Faso","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/37/burkina-faso"]," including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["yellow fever"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue and malaria"]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Burkina Faso"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities in Burkina Faso are very limited. For serious medical treatment, evacuation to Europe is necessary. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and medical evacuation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Burkina Faso","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/burkina-faso-doctors-and-medical-facilities/burkina-faso-list-of-doctors-and-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Ouagadougou"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 18"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 18"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 17"]},{"k":"p","s":["Outside Ouagadougou, the emergency services are unlikely to respond."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take local advice instead."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Burkina%20Faso"]," and ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Burkina%20Faso"]," in Burkina Faso"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Burkina Faso","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/burkina-faso-bereavement-death-abroad/burkina-faso-bereavement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Burkina Faso","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/burkina-faso-prisoners-pack/information-pack-for-british-nationals-arrested-or-detained-in-burkina-faso"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/burkina-faso/burkina-faso"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/burkina-faso/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":16650,"change":"New information about the death penalty in Burkina Faso (‘Safety and security’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/congo":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"fc405269566c29e3ce36ca2d8aaf0b08a8e29b3219402223fbb2418389ac2674","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/congo","bytes":45266,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Congo travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-21T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-10-27T12:00:20+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Republic of Congo-Central African Republic border area in Likouala Region"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to within 50km of the Republic of Congo-Central African Republic border in Likouala Region."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/congo/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/congo/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Congo’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in the Republic of Congo set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the Republic of Congo Embassy in the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 0203 691 5979"]},{"k":"p","s":["Email: contactambacouki@gmail.com"]},{"k":"p","s":["Address: 83 Victoria Street, London, SW1H OHW"]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport must be valid for the duration of your stay. No additional period of validity is needed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to enter the Republic of Congo."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["Apply for a visa before you travel. Contact the ",["Republic of Congo Embassy in the UK","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/foreign-embassies-in-the-uk"]," for more information."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To pass border control in the Republic of Congo, you must have certificates to prove you’ve had:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a yellow fever vaccination, due to a risk of yellow fever transmission"]},{"k":"p","s":["For more details about health entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Republic of Congo guide","https://www.travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/55/congo#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers arriving in the Republic of Congo may be subject to enhanced health screening measures due to the ongoing Ebola outbreak centred in the Democratic Republic of Congo."]},{"k":"p","s":["The World Health Organisation (WHO) has ",["declared this a Public Health Emergency of International Concern","https://www.who.int/news/item/17-05-2026-epidemic-of-ebola-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-and-uganda-determined-a-public-health-emergency-of-international-concern"],". ",["Check entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice"]," for the country you’re travelling to or transiting."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of the Republic of Congo. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of the Republic of Congo","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/congo/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in the Republic of Congo"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in the Republic of Congo, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Demonstrations happen occasionally. In the past, demonstrations have become violent. Even when they are peaceful there is a risk of violence. Avoid any areas with demonstrations."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Pool Region has historically been an area of conflict between Government Forces and the Ninja insurgent group. Live conflict has not been reported since both parties signed a ceasefire agreement in 2017. Violent clashes could arise again with little or no notice in response to political events. Be vigilant for reports of local unrest."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been reports of crime, particularly opportunistic crime such as pickpocketing, particularly in Brazzaville and Pointe Noire, and criminals may target foreigners."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care of your belongings, particularly in Brazzaville and Pointe Noire. To reduce your personal risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid walking in the streets after dark"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not carry large amounts of cash or valuables"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid isolated areas, including beaches"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vehicle crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals may target your car. Take extra precautions against criminals targeting your vehicle, especially when travelling outside urban centres and anywhere in the Pool Region and Mouyondzi District. Reduce the risk of carjacking and break-ins by:"]},{"k":"li","s":["locking doors and keeping windows closed, including whilst travelling"]},{"k":"li","s":["not driving away from main routes"]},{"k":"li","s":["always parking in a secure location"]},{"k":"li","s":["making journeys during daylight hours in rural areas"]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police may ask you for ID. Always carry a colour copy of your passport, including your visa entry stamp. If you live in Congo, also always carry a colour copy of your residency card."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in the Republic of Congo, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in the Republic of Congo. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience, a higher minimum age and holding an IDP."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some road conditions, particularly in remote parts of the country may be poor, particularly during the wet season from November to May. Reduce the risks of rural travel by using a well-maintained 4-wheel drive vehicle with necessary supplies. Travelling in convoy and in daylight will reduce the risk of being stranded if a breakdown or accident happens."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Checkpoints"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent vehicle checkpoints in the Republic of Congo, which can be poorly marked. If you’re asked for documents at a checkpoint, stay in your vehicle and show them through a closed window."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["UK Air Safety List (ASL)","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/uk-air-safety-list"]," lists all known airlines in the Republic of Congo that do not meet international safety standards and are banned from operating commercial air services to, from, and within the UK. Check the UK Air Safety List when considering which airlines to fly with. The list is maintained by the Department for Transport, based on advice from the ",["UK Civil Aviation Authority","https://www.caa.co.uk/Commercial-Industry/Airlines/Licensing/Requirements-and-guidance/Third-Country-Operator-Certificates"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rail travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["A passenger rail service operates between Brazzaville and Pointe Noire however, the service is often slow and unreliable."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Boat travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The river border crossing between Brazzaville and Kinshasa can close without warning. The ferry stops running in late afternoon, does not run on Sunday and may be cancelled when there is bad weather. Check before travelling."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of the Republic of Congo. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/congo"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/congo/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Republic of Congo-Central African Republic border area in Likouala Region"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel within 50km of the Republic of Congo-Central African Republic (CAR) border in Likouala Region."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of violence, crime and insecurity in this area due to instability in CAR."]},{"k":"h","s":["The Pool Region"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some areas in the Pool region have historically been areas of conflict between the government and the Ninja insurgent group. There have not been any reports of live conflict since a ceasefire was agreed in 2017, however a risk remains of violent clashes breaking out with little or no notice, particularly in the districts of Boko, Kindamba, Kinkala, Mayama and Mindouli."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["There’s no central number for emergency services. Check for local medical facilities and carry contact details with you."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for the Republic of Congo","https://www.travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/55/congo#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see how to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in the Republic of Congo","https://www.travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/55/congo#Vaccine_Recommendations"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["yellow fever"]},{"k":"li","s":["schistosomiasis"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria and dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["mpox"]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you take medication, bring enough for your time in the Republic of Congo and make sure it is clearly labelled. Bring a copy of any prescription."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in the Republic of Congo"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities in the country are limited, particularly in rural areas. Medical evacuation is likely to be necessary for all but the most basic treatments. If you become ill while in the Republic of Congo or straight after leaving the country, get immediate medical advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have adequate travel and medical insurance to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation; this should specifically include the very high costs of evacuation by air ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in the Republic of Congo","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners-in-the-republic-of-congo"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in the Republic of Congo"]},{"k":"p","s":["There’s no central number for emergency services in the Republic of Congo. You can report crimes to local police on 06 665 4804. Few police will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check for local medical facilities and carry contact details with you."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone numbers can be unreliable."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Congo"],", ",["funeral directors","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/list-of-funeral-directors-in-republic-of-congo/list-of-funeraldirectors-in-republic-of-congo"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=congo"]," in the Republic of Congo"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in the Republic of Congo","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/republic-of-congo-bereavement-packinformation"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in the Republic of Congo","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/explanation-of-the-legal-and-prison-system-to-british-nationals"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/congo/british-embassy-kinshasa"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/congo/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":12378,"change":"Updated information about vaccine requirements for border control (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/kredibilitas-indonesia-diuji-saat-bencana-dan-asap-karhutla-melintasi-batas-negara-294803":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"14e6889a6b1f370e50f6ef369b0fe2e4ee7832feb37f27428ebd884bbb29d7c5","read":"https://theconversation.com/kredibilitas-indonesia-diuji-saat-bencana-dan-asap-karhutla-melintasi-batas-negara-294803","bytes":182544,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Kredibilitas Indonesia diuji saat bencana dan asap karhutla melintasi batas negara","by":[{"n":"Jessica Martha","r":"Dosen, Universitas Katolik Parahyangan"}],"pub":"2026-10-21T10:02:13Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Sepanjang 2026, kebakaran hutan dan lahan (karhutla) di Indonesia kembali memicu krisis lingkungan dan kesehatan yang dampaknya ",["melampaui batas negara","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/clyqw44w142o"],". ",["Analisis Greenpeace Indonesia","https://www.greenpeace.org/indonesia/siaran-pers/67885/warga-sesak-karena-kabut-asap-namun-pemerintah-gagal-paham-akar-masalah-karhutla-gambut"]," menemukan 5.540 titik sumber asap di 22 provinsi selama 8 Agustus hingga 20 September."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kabut asap telah menyebar ke Malaysia, Singapura, Brunei Darussalam, hingga Filipina, Thailand, Vietnam, dan Kamboja–mengganggu aktivitas warga sehari-hari."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Di Sarawak","https://news.mongabay.com/2026/09/in-southeast-asia-residents-grapple-with-life-under-indonesias-wildfire-haze/amp"],", memburuknya kualitas udara memicu lonjakan kasus asma hingga 259%. Sementara itu, tingkat polusi yang tercatat di Manila dilaporkan lebih dari empat kali lipat ambang batas aman yang ditetapkan oleh Organisasi Kesehatan Dunia (WHO)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di Indonesia sendiri, kasus infeksi saluran pernapasan akut (ISPA) yang dikaitkan dengan karhutla di tujuh provinsi ",["mencapai 277.075 kasus","https://www.antaranews.com/berita/5785085/kemenkes-catat-277-ribu-ispa-per-oktober-kuatkan-respons-kesehatan"]," per 12 Oktober, lebih dari dua kali lipat angka pada 9 September."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Kasus ISPA meroket: Asap karhutla jadi ancaman senyap di daerah yang jauh dari pusat kebakaran","https://theconversation.com/kasus-ispa-meroket-asap-karhutla-jadi-ancaman-senyap-di-daerah-yang-jauh-dari-pusat-kebakaran-294660"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Kejadian ini menyoroti tantangan yang lebih besar untuk Indonesia: ketika krisis dalam negeri menjadi perhatian internasional, dampaknya tidak hanya kerusakan fisik. Krisis ini juga dapat memengaruhi hubungan diplomatik, kepercayaan publik, dan persepsi negara lain terhadap Indonesia sebagai negara yang bertanggung jawab."]},{"k":"p","s":["Oleh karena itu, cara Indonesia menanggapi dan mengomunikasikan krisis ini menjadi sangat penting, tidak hanya untuk penanganan bencana, tetapi juga untuk menjaga reputasinya pada kancah global."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ketika krisis dalam negeri menarik perhatian internasional"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dampak karhutla tidak berhenti pada kesehatan masyarakat. Karhutla juga mengganggu aktivitas ekonomi dan transportasi. Menurut ",["Reuters","https://www.reuters.com/business/environment/indonesias-burned-land-doubles-september-fires-rage-data-shows-2026-10-20/"],", lebih dari 1.400 penerbangan dibatalkan atau ditunda akibat karhutla sejak Agustus 2026."]},{"k":"p","s":["Respons negara tetangga menunjukkan bahwa persoalan ini tidak lagi terbatas pada dampak lingkungan. ",["Badan Lingkungan Hidup Nasional Singapura (NEA)","https://www.straitstimes.com/singapore/nea-issues-notices-to-three-more-companies-in-indonesia-over-haze-role"]," mengeluarkan pemberitahuan kepada sepuluh perusahaan di Indonesia. NEA meminta perusahaan-perusahaan tersebut memadamkan api, menghentikan aktivitas pembakaran, dan menyusun langkah pencegahan agar kebakaran tidak terulang."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sebelumnya, tekanan diplomatik juga muncul dari anggota parlemen Malaysia, ",["Syed Saddiq Syed Abdul Rahman","https://www.nst.com.my/news/nation/2026/10/1554575/syed-saddiq-calls-asean-pressure-indonesia-over-haze"],". Ia mengajak negara-negara ASEAN mengajukan protes diplomatik kepada Indonesia karena dinilai belum berbuat cukup untuk mengendalikan karhutla."]},{"k":"p","s":["Rangkaian peristiwa ini menunjukkan bahwa karhutla dapat memengaruhi hubungan Indonesia dengan negara lainnya. Bagi Indonesia yang ingin berperan lebih besar di tingkat regional dan global, krisis ini menjadi ujian kredibilitas dalam mengangani risiko lingkungan lintas batas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kredibilitas tidak hanya ditentukan oleh penanganan di lapangan, tetapi juga oleh cara pemerintah menyampaikan informasi, merespons kekhawatiran, dan menjelaskan upaya yang sedang dilakukan. Komunikasi menjadi penting karena ikut membentuk persepsi dan kepercayaan publik internasional terhadap Indonesia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lalu, ketika karhutla melintasi batas negara, bagaimana komunikasi pemerintah Indonesia dapat melindungi masyarakat terdampak sekaligus menjaga kepercayaan internasional?"]},{"k":"h","s":["Komunikasi krisis sebagai diplomasi publik"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Ingrid d’Hooghe","https://doi.org/10.1163/9789004283954_009"],", peneliti senior dan mantan Kepala Clingendael China Centre, menjelaskan bahwa ketika krisis dalam negeri menjadi perhatian internasional, pemerintah perlu berkomunikasi dengan masyarakat di dalam maupun luar negeri melalui tiga jenis informasi: informasi untuk menghadapi dampak fisik, informasi untuk menghadapi dampak psikologis, dan komunikasi untuk memulihkan reputasi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Informasi untuk menghadapi dampak fisik berupa panduan untuk mengurangi risiko. Dalam konteks karhutla, informasi ini mencakup pembaruan kualitas udara, wilayah terdampak, risiko kesehatan, dan langkah-langkah perlindungan yang dapat dilakukan masyarakat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketika ",["kualitas udara Pontianak memasuki kategori berbahaya","https://www.cnnindonesia.com/teknologi/20260901090426-641-1398601/kualitas-udara-pontianak-masuk-kategori-berbahaya-paling-buruk-di-ri"],", masyarakat membutuhkan informasi jelas mengenai risiko paparan asap dan cara mengurangi dampaknya terhadap kesehatan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Menurut ",["WHO","https://www.who.int/news-room/questions-and-answers/item/air-pollution-personal-interventions-and-risk-communication?utm_source=chatgpt.com"],", tersedianya informasi kualitas udara dan imbauan kesehatan yang mudah dipahami dapat membantu masyarakat mengambil langkah untuk mengurangi dampak polusi dan melindungi kesehatan, terutama kelompok rentan seperti anak-anak, lansia, dan orang dengan penyakit pernapasan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Informasi untuk menghadapi dampak psikologis berfungsi untuk mengurangi kecemasan dan ketidakpastian. Dalam situasi karhutla yang berkepanjangan, masyarakat memerlukan pembaruan informasi yang konsisten mengenai upaya pemadaman, perkembangan kondisi asap, dan langkah pemerintah untuk melindungi warga. Komunikasi juga perlu menunjukkan kepedulian terhadap kondisi masyarakat yang terdampak, bukan sekadar menyampaikan informasi teknis."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dampak komunikasi krisis juga melampaui batas negara. Informasi yang konsisten dan disampaikan tepat waktu memungkinkan pemerintah negara tetangga menilai risiko dan mengoordinasikan respons mereka masing-masing. Sebaliknya, sikap diam, informasi yang simpang siur, atau keterlambatan komunikasi dapat menyulitkan dan memengaruhi kepercayaan negara lain terhadap penanganan krisis oleh Indonesia."]},{"k":"h","s":["Krisis yang berbeda, tantangan diplomatik yang berbeda"]},{"k":"p","s":["Jenis informasi ketiga, yakni komunikasi untuk memulihkan reputasi, menghadirkan tantangan tersendiri karena tidak semua bencana membawa dampak yang sama terhadap reputasi negara."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Pemulihan reputasi","https://doi.org/10.1163/9789004283954_009"]," merujuk pada strategi penyampaian informasi dan komunikasi untuk memperbaiki citra negara yang telanjur rusak. Hal ini semakin relevan ketika krisis berkaitan dengan tindakan yang dapat dipertanggungjawabkan kepada pihak tertentu, kurangnya upaya pencegahan, atau penanganan yang tidak memadai sehingga negara dianggap bertanggung jawab dan dikritik."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kebakaran hutan menghadirkan tantangan berbeda karena ",["sebagian besar kebakaran disebabkan","https://theconversation.com/borneo-forest-fires-spike-again-why-el-nino-isnt-the-sole-culprit-290334"]," oleh aktivitas manusia, kelalaian, dan lemahnya penegakan hukum."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Mengapa sanksi pelaku karhutla amat timpang dengan kerugian berantai yang ditimbulkannya?","https://theconversation.com/mengapa-sanksi-pelaku-karhutla-amat-timpang-dengan-kerugian-berantai-yang-ditimbulkannya-290256"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam kasus seperti ini, sekadar mengaitkan kebakaran dengan cuaca kering atau ",["fenomena Super El Niño","https://news.detik.com/berita/d-8628464/bmkg-ungkap-penyebab-karhutla-di-kalimantan-iklim-kering-efek-el-nino"]," dapat menimbulkan reaksi negatif di luar negeri. Bagi masyarakat di Kuching atau Manila yang menghirup asap, penjelasan menggunakan kondisi iklim bisa terdengar seperti alasan untuk menghindari tanggung jawab."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kata-kata saja ",["tidak cukup untuk memulihkan reputasi","https://doi.org/10.1016/S0363-8111(97)90023-0"]," ketika masyarakat menuntut tindakan nyata. Pemerintah perlu menegakkan hukum lingkungan, mengusut pihak yang bertanggung jawab, memperkuat pencegahan kebakaran, dan mengatasi kondisi yang memungkinkan kebakaran terus berulang."]},{"k":"p","s":["Perbedaan ini sangat krusial dalam hubungan diplomatik. Bencana alam menguji kemampuan Indonesia menanggapi ancaman yang tidak dapat dihindari, sedangkan krisis kebakaran yang terus berulang juga menguji kesediaan Indonesia dan negara-negara tetangganya untuk berkomunikasi secara terbuka mengenai tanggung jawab bersama atas risiko yang melintasi perbatasan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Apa yang perlu disampaikan dan dilakukan Indonesia?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bagi Indonesia, komunikasi bencana bukan sekadar upaya menyampaikan informasi kepada masyarakat. Komunikasi juga merupakan bagian dari diplomasi publik."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pemerintah perlu menyampaikan informasi secara tepat, terbuka, dan konsisten. Namun, komunikasi harus berjalan seiring dengan tindakan nyata: melindungi masyarakat, menunjukkan akuntabilitas, dan keseriusan dalam melakukan pencegahan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pada akhirnya, reputasi Indonesia di mata dunia selama krisis tidak hanya ditentukan oleh apa yang disampaikan pemerintah, tetapi juga oleh keselarasan antara pernyataan dan tindakan yang benar-benar dilakukan."]}],"chars":7577},"https://theconversation.com/fasilitas-ada-tapi-sulit-diakses-mengapa-pelayanan-publik-ramah-difabel-masih-langka-di-indonesia-293693":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"61d2fe602c2c6d701b3afbc145d05aff569221362c33bfed280fd1d58e98fb26","read":"https://theconversation.com/fasilitas-ada-tapi-sulit-diakses-mengapa-pelayanan-publik-ramah-difabel-masih-langka-di-indonesia-293693","bytes":179672,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Fasilitas ada, tapi sulit diakses: Mengapa pelayanan publik ramah difabel masih langka di Indonesia","by":[{"n":"Muhammad Dzulfikar Al Ghofiqi","r":"Dosen dan Peneliti di Departemen Administrasi Publik, Fakultas Ilmu Sosial dan Ilmu Politik, Universitas Airlangga, Universitas Airlangga"}],"pub":"2026-10-21T01:36:27Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["● Aturan dan fasilitas belum menjamin layanan publik yang aksesibel bagi difabel."]},{"k":"p","s":["● Pelibatan komunitas difabel membantu pemerintah menemukan dan memperbaiki hambatan layanan."]},{"k":"p","s":["● Partisipasi harus dilembagakan agar perbaikan layanan tidak bergantung pada individu."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sudah sedekade ",["Undang-Undang Nomor 8 Tahun 2016","https://peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/37251/uu-no-8-tahun-2016"]," tentang Penyandang Disabilitas disahkan, tapi kondisi orang difabel tak banyak berubah."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ragam persoalan warisan dahulu kala seperti jalur pemandu yang terputus, informasi yang tidak tersedia dalam format aksesibel, dan petugas yang kesulitan berkomunikasi dengan pengguna difabel masih jadi makanan sehari-hari."]},{"k":"p","s":["Masalahnya bukan semata-mata kekurangan fasilitas. Pemerintah juga perlu memastikan orang disabilitas dilibatkan sejak layanan dirancang, bukan baru didengarkan setelah masalah muncul. Tanpa keterlibatan pengguna, kebijakan yang terlihat memadai di atas kertas bisa gagal menjawab kebutuhan warga."]},{"k":"p","s":["Melansir ",["Ombudsman RI","https://ombudsman.go.id/news/r/wujudkan-pelayanan-publik-inklusif-ombudsman-ri-dan-knd-perkuat-sinergi-pengawasan?utm_source=chatgpt.com"],", laporan terkait disabilitas meningkat setiap tahun. Sementara itu, ",["Komisi Nasional Disabilitas","https://ombudsman.go.id/pers/r/wujudkan-pelayanan-publik-inklusif-ombudsman-ri-dan-knd-perkuat-sinergi-pengawasan"]," menilai pemenuhan hak penyandang disabilitas dalam pelayanan publik masih belum optimal."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pengalaman Mal Pelayanan Publik (MPP) Kabupaten Lamongan, Jawa Timur, menunjukkan bagaimana keterlibatan komunitas difabel dapat membantu memperbaiki layanan."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Riset kami","https://doi.org/10.1002/pad.70074"],", yang melibatkan 27 informan dan diterbitkan dalam jurnal Public Administration and Development pada 2026, menemukan bahwa perbaikan membutuhkan kapasitas pemerintah sekaligus komunitas yang mampu menyampaikan kritik dan mengawal tindak lanjutnya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["4 tantangan pelayanan publik berbasis digital di Indonesia","https://theconversation.com/4-tantangan-pelayanan-publik-berbasis-digital-di-indonesia-203848"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Standar pemerintah tak sesuai kebutuhan warga"]},{"k":"p","s":["Saat MPP Lamongan mulai beroperasi, pemerintah telah memiliki standar operasional prosedur (SOP) layanan prioritas. Namun, komunitas difabel tidak dilibatkan sejak awal penyusunannya. Akibatnya, rancangan layanan belum sepenuhnya menjawab kebutuhan pengguna."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tak ada jalur pemandu dan informasi Braille untuk tuna netra. Teman tuli kesulitan berkomunikasi karena sedikit petugas yang memahami bahasa isyarat. Sementara itu, disabilitas fisik dipaksa melewati bidang miring yang curam dan mendatangi loket di lantai dua."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kondisi tersebut memperlihatkan kelemahan birokrasi yang terlalu mengandalkan kepatuhan administratif alias cuma sekadar memenuhi kewajiban. Keberadaan SOP dan fasilitas tidak otomatis membuktikan bahwa layanan dapat digunakan semua orang."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bagi warga yang datang untuk mengurus dokumen, mengakses layanan tanpa bantuan dan panduan yang sesuai justru membuat antrean makin mengular. Pemerintah seharusnya mengukur keberhasilan layanan dari pengalaman pengguna, bukan hanya dari fasilitas yang tersedia atau prosedur yang telah ditetapkan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Temuan ini sejalan dengan ",["tinjauan sistematis","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/padm.13049?__cf_chl_rt_tk=RFT7PekkjGmTbt0fKdx51myyKANimenE6O_SxEbHxL8-1791981261-1.0.1.1-SWlKLwpmyqvzv7z45GyHJ9B_NKBLZp7s7bbZ0tJm6Yc"]," yang mengkaji 119 penelitian tentang inklusi warga dalam layanan publik. Kajian tersebut menyoroti pentingnya memahami bagaimana interaksi warga dengan layanan membentuk pengalaman inklusi, sekaligus bagaimana hambatan administratif dapat menghalanginya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Mengapa layanan kesehatan untuk disabilitas di Indonesia masih belum maksimal?","https://theconversation.com/mengapa-layanan-kesehatan-untuk-disabilitas-di-indonesia-masih-belum-maksimal-247473"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Ubah keluhan menjadi perubahan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Di Lamongan, komunitas difabel berupaya mengubah pengalaman individual menjadi tuntutan bersama."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pada Desember 2020, melalui ",["Festival Inklusi","https://timesindonesia.co.id/peristiwa-daerah/314234/penyandang-disabilitas-inginkan-guiding-block-di-semua-trotoar-kota-lamongan"],", mereka menyuarakan kebutuhan agar jalur pemandu tunanetra diperluas ke seluruh trotoar kota. Jalur yang tersedia di alun-alun belum menjamin perjalanan yang aman ketika akses terputus di lokasi lain."]},{"k":"p","s":["Berbagai organisasi kemudian menghimpun aspirasi melalui Forum Perlindungan dan Pemenuhan Hak Penyandang Disabilitas (FP2HD). Forum ini membantu komunitas menyusun usulan, berkomunikasi dengan pemerintah, dan mengawal respons atas hambatan yang mereka alami."]},{"k":"p","s":["Melalui forum konsultasi publik, masukan komunitas turut mendorong perubahan alur pelayanan yang dimulai dari area parkir, penyediaan ruang layanan khusus di lantai satu, penempatan petugas yang dibekali keterampilan bahasa isyarat, serta pengembangan kompetensi pegawai dan dukungan anggaran."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Penelitian tentang aksesibilitas layanan puskesmas di Bandung","https://knia.stialanbandung.ac.id/index.php/knia/article/view/595"]," juga menunjukkan pentingnya pelibatan masyarakat dalam perbaikan fasilitas publik. Namun, tentunya partisipasi ini tidak boleh menjadi cara pemerintah memindahkan tanggung jawab kepada warga."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["6 penghalang keterlibatan penyandang disabilitas dalam proses pembangunan","https://theconversation.com/6-penghalang-keterlibatan-penyandang-disabilitas-dalam-proses-pembangunan-108176"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Partisipasi harus jadi kewajiban kelembagaan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pengalaman Lamongan menunjukkan bahwa kritik komunitas dapat membantu pemerintah mengenali kekurangan yang luput dari perencanaan. Namun, perbaikan akan rapuh jika bergantung pada pejabat tertentu atau kegigihan segelintir aktivis."]},{"k":"p","s":["Karena itu, pemerintah perlu melembagakan partisipasi melalui tiga langkah."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pertama, libatkan organisasi difabel sejak penyusunan dan evaluasi SOP, pembangunan fasilitas, hingga penentuan anggaran. Pengujian layanan harus melibatkan pengguna dengan ragam disabilitas karena kebutuhan mereka berbeda-beda."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kedua, setiap masukan harus memiliki penanggung jawab, tenggat waktu, dan tindak lanjut yang dapat diperiksa publik. Pemerintah juga perlu menjelaskan alasan jika usulan belum dapat dilaksanakan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketiga, sediakan forum konsultasi yang aksesibel dan dukungan bagi komunitas untuk memantau layanan secara independen. Kritik tidak boleh bergantung pada kedekatan komunitas dengan pejabat yang sedang menjabat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Riset satu kasus tidak dapat mewakili seluruh Indonesia. Namun, pelajarannya relevan: pemerintah tidak cukup mengklaim layanan telah inklusif hanya karena aturan dan fasilitas tersedia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ukuran keberhasilannya adalah apakah orang difabel dapat memperoleh informasi, berkomunikasi dengan petugas, mengakses fasilitas, dan menyelesaikan urusan secara aman dan bermartabat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Layanan publik baru benar-benar inklusif ketika penyandang disabilitas bukan sekadar penerima layanan, melainkan turut menentukan bagaimana layanan dirancang, dijalankan, dan dievaluasi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Mendorong penelitian inklusif: Penyandang disabilitas perlu terlibat aktif, bukan hanya sebagai objek","https://theconversation.com/mendorong-penelitian-inklusif-penyandang-disabilitas-perlu-terlibat-aktif-bukan-hanya-sebagai-objek-242911"]]}],"chars":6003},"https://theconversation.com/wab-kinew-wants-the-indian-act-gone-its-an-opportunity-to-trade-old-colonial-rules-for-new-nation-to-nation-relations-295434":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"3ad6a91538194c83dc1fc1a839cd545ea61f45cd3d693ca92fc463b064e6ef71","read":"https://theconversation.com/wab-kinew-wants-the-indian-act-gone-its-an-opportunity-to-trade-old-colonial-rules-for-new-nation-to-nation-relations-295434","bytes":189621,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Wab Kinew wants the Indian Act gone: It’s an opportunity to trade old colonial rules for new nation-to-nation relations","by":[{"n":"Frank Deer","r":"Professor, Faculty of Education, University of Manitoba"}],"pub":"2026-11-02T16:31:27Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Manitoba Premier Wab Kinew recently ",["called for the abolition of the Indian Act","https://www.cjme.com/2026/10/26/kinew-calls-on-carney-to-abolish-the-indian-act-at-meeting-with-chiefs/"]," during a meeting in Ottawa with Prime Minister Mark Carney, provincial premiers and First Nations leaders."]},{"k":"p","s":["Holding up his ",["Indian status card","https://www.sac-isc.gc.ca/eng/1100100032374/1572457769548"],", Kinew questioned why Canada continues to maintain legislation that classifies Indigenous people according to a federally administered system of identity."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some have called his remarks a ",["distraction from the conversation on resource extraction","https://music.youtube.com/watch?v=jwE6pb9KLlI"],". A few Conservatives have called it ",["an empty academic exercise","https://www.winnipegfreepress.com/canada/2026/10/27/carney-says-ottawas-indian-act-review-might-not-end-up-abolishing-the-law"],". And still others have called it bold."]},{"k":"p","s":["But no matter what you think of his motivations, Kinew’s call ",["raises important questions about the relationship between First Nations and the Canadian state","https://truenorthaid.ca/indigenous-self-determination/"],", particularly concerning Indigenous nationhood and self-determination."]},{"k":"h","s":["What is the Indian Act?"]},{"k":"p","s":["First ",["enacted in 1876","https://yellowheadinstitute.org/2026/the-indian-act-exit-150/"],", the Indian Act consolidated earlier colonial legislation intended to regulate the lives of First Nations Peoples. The legislation established federal authority over reserve lands, political governance and the legal recognition of Indigenous identity."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["Canadian government acknowledges","https://cirnac.gc.ca/eng/1307460755710/1536862806124"]," the legislation was founded on the assumption that First Nations required federal guardianship until they could be integrated into Canadian society."]},{"k":"p","s":["The consequences of this approach have been profound. The ",["Indian Act","https://thecanadianencyclopedia.ca/en/article/indian-act"]," and associated federal policies undermine traditional systems of governance. Historically, it has restricted cultural and ceremonial practices."]},{"k":"p","s":["It ",["contributed to the assimilationist policies that supported the residential school system","https://www.facinghistory.org/en-ca/resource-library/historical-background-indian-act-indian-residential-schools"],". The legislation also established discriminatory provisions that historically ",["deprived some First Nations women and their descendants of Indian status","https://thecanadianencyclopedia.ca/en/article/bill-c-31"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite numerous amendments, ",["the Indian Act continues to influence how numerous First Nations are governed. It still determines how their members are recognized under Canadian law","https://www.cbc.ca/radio/unreserved/how-the-indian-act-continues-to-impact-the-lives-of-first-nation-people-1.5614187"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["First Nations Peoples remain skeptical"]},{"k":"p","s":["Kinew’s remarks invite consideration of a fundamental contradiction. While ",["Canada professes a commitment to nation-to-nation relations","https://www.justice.gc.ca/eng/csj-sjc/principles-principes.html"],", much of its relationships with First Nations continues to operate through legislation premised upon federal authority over them."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kinew’s call suggests First Nations should work with the Canadian government on the abolishment of the Indian Act and toward a replacement."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are good reasons for First Nations Peoples to remain skeptical of the federal government’s commitment to working with them. Canada’s history is marked by repeated failures by governments to honour First Nations rights, treaties and political authority."]},{"k":"p","s":["For example, the ",["1990 Oka Crisis","https://cirnac.gc.ca/eng/1307460755710/1536862806124#chp6"]," was an episode in which Mohawk people defended ancestral lands against proposed development; the confrontation led to my First Nation existing under military occupation."]},{"k":"p","s":["More recently, the proposed ",["Bill C-39","https://afn.ca/legislation-to-watch/bill-c-39/"],", intended to accelerate major project approvals, raises concerns about whether expedited decision-making on development affecting traditional lands and rights sidesteps First Nations consultation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Such concerns raise questions about Canada’s willingness to recognize First Nations nationhood. Against this historical backdrop, promises of reconciliation and nation-to-nation relations warrant careful scrutiny."]},{"k":"h","s":["First Nations: Distinct political communities"]},{"k":"p","s":["A genuine nation-to-nation relationship requires more than recognition of Indigenous rights within Canada. It requires recognition that First Nations are distinct political communities possessing their own histories, laws, governing traditions and understandings of nationhood."]},{"k":"p","s":["A nation-to-nation relationship should be grounded in mutual respect and the right of nations to determine their own political futures, a principle affirmed by the ",["United Nations Declaration on the Rights of Indigenous Peoples","https://www.justice.gc.ca/eng/declaration/decl_doc.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["Indian Act","https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/acts/I-5/"]," has never been particularly well-suited for this purpose. Established as an instrument of colonial administration, it presumes that significant aspects of First Nations political life should be governed through legislation created and maintained by the federal government. This arrangement is difficult to reconcile with the principle that First Nations possess an inherent right to govern themselves."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Kinew’s call to abolish the act","https://www.aptnnews.ca/national-news/manitoba-premier-wab-kinew-calls-on-prime-minister-to-abolish-the-indian-act-at-meeting-with-chiefs/"]," may present an important opportunity, one in which questions about what legislation might replace the Indian Act should be discussed."]},{"k":"p","s":["But more fundamentally, it should encourage First Nations Peoples to consider the realities of the Indian Act and how they understand their own nationhood and the political relationships they want to establish with Canada."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emancipation isn’t charity"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is where the idea of native auto-emancipation becomes particularly relevant. In 1882, Jewish writer ",["Leo Pinsker argued in his 1882 pamphlet Auto-Emancipation","https://www.posenlibrary.com/entry/autoemancipation-birth-jewish-nationalism"]," that Jewish emancipation could not depend exclusively upon the goodwill or recognition of other nations. Jewish people needed to take responsibility for their own collective political future."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although the historical circumstances of Jewish and Indigenous Peoples differ considerably, Pinsker’s argument offers a useful point of reflection."]},{"k":"p","s":["For generations, First Nations Peoples have been encouraged, and sometimes compelled, to understand their place within Canadian political and social institutions. This integrationist approach risks making Indigenous nationhood dependent upon the extent to which it is accommodated or recognized by Canada rather than upon the ",["inherent right of Indigenous Peoples to self-determination","https://www.justice.gc.ca/eng/declaration/themes.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Native auto-emancipation suggests a different starting point. Rather than asking how First Nations might find greater recognition within Canada and its institutions, Indigenous Peoples should continue to ask what it means to belong to their own nations."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is not a new question. For instance, in the 2009 ",["Peace, Power, and Righteousness: an Indigenous Manifesto,","https://global.oup.com/academic/product/peace-power-righteousness-9780195430516"],", Kahnawà:ke author Taiaiake Alfred explores the importance of Indigenous Peoples returning to their traditional political and governmental ways."]},{"k":"p","s":["To engage with such change would be to increase attention on such things as Indigenous languages, laws, histories, territories and responsibilities. The ",["United Nations Declaration on the Rights of Indigenous Peoples","https://laws.justice.gc.ca/eng/acts/U-2.2/FullText.html"],", particularly Article 33, affirms the right of Indigenous Peoples to determine their own identity, membership and political institutions."]},{"k":"h","s":["Avoiding a reliance on Canada"]},{"k":"p","s":["Abolishing the Indian Act might create opportunities for meaningful change, provided that ",["existing rights and protections are preserved","https://www.btpm.org/ontario-news/2026-10-28/canadian-indigenous-leaders-meet-to-discuss-reforming-abolishing-divisive-indian-act"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the more fundamental transformation may involve First Nations Peoples continuing to orient their identities, responsibilities and political leanings toward their own nationhood, and to avoid relying on Canada to define the terms of their political existence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some may believe Kinew’s call to abolish the Indian Act was bold. Some believe that ",["his message was presumptuous and that he may have been attempting to speak for other First Nations people","https://www.ctvnews.ca/politics/article/pm-carney-says-its-time-to-move-beyond-indian-act/"],". But any card-carrying Status Indian is entitled to opine on the continued existence of the Indian Act."]},{"k":"p","s":["One way of addressing the Manitoba premier’s words is to allow them to fuel a conversation. If First Nations are interested in establishing a real nation-to-nation relationship with Canada, one where their nationhood, sovereignty and inherent right to self-determination are acknowledged and respected, then the extent to which the Indian Act enables such a relationship should be carefully considered."]}],"chars":7501},"https://theconversation.com/national-ground-stop-response-highlights-critical-errors-in-public-reassurance-saying-nothing-nefarious-did-the-opposite-of-quelling-public-concern-296663":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"981f7b5482e6408bc7c2235b1044244df1a83d37989f9021c65a05fb5fe42ae1","read":"https://theconversation.com/national-ground-stop-response-highlights-critical-errors-in-public-reassurance-saying-nothing-nefarious-did-the-opposite-of-quelling-public-concern-296663","bytes":184410,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"National ground stop response highlights critical errors in public reassurance – saying ‘nothing nefarious’ did the opposite of quelling public concern","by":[{"n":"Shannon A. Bowen","r":"Professor of Journalism and Mass Communications, University of South Carolina"}],"pub":"2026-11-14T18:46:42Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":[["Thousands of travelers were stranded","https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/11/14/us/faa-nationwide-ground-stop-flights"]," on Nov. 13, 2026, when the Federal Aviation Administration grounded all domestic flights in the U.S. because of what they said were ",["failures in decades-old air traffic communications systems","https://www.kake.com/news/national/you-will-have-more-of-these-unless-system-upgraded-duffy-says-of-outage-that-led/article_4cbc8ca8-cbe2-4119-af1e-6b0de1def505.html"],". ",["Crisis communications expert Shannon A. Bowen","https://sc.edu/study/colleges_schools/cic/faculty-staff/bowen_shannon.php"],", a scholar at the University of South Carolina’s College of Information and Communications, spoke with The Conversation’s Politics and Legal Affairs Editor, Naomi Schalit, about how the Trump administration handled the first day of the crisis."]},{"k":"p","s":["This interview has been edited for length and clarity."]},{"k":"p","s":["Is there a first principle in crisis communications?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The first principle would be to react quickly and react with accuracy, react with everything you know at the moment, truthfully, but always react quickly. Because if you delay until you gather information, a vacuum will ensue. Information fills that vacuum that may not be accurate. And so that’s the enemy of accurate crisis communication, but you want to always speak quickly and be the most authoritative and definitive source, even if very little information is known."]},{"k":"p","s":["What did we see on the day of the ground stop?"]},{"k":"p","s":["A crisis unfolded and to the administration’s credit, ",["they did react very quickly","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Yuwrrs8MBPc"],", in a way that offered the information that was known at the time, even though not a lot was known about why the ground stop was issued until later."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’re speaking about the ",["short press conference that afternoon","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Yuwrrs8MBPc"]," with Department of Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin?"]},{"k":"p","s":["He did keep saying that ",["nothing nefarious was at hand","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YBLQm2dDl6Y"],". And for a crisis communication scholar, ",["you would not want to introduce the idea","https://www.researchgate.net/publication/397432409_Principles_of_Effective_Crisis_Communication"]," that something nefarious was at hand, unless, indeed, something nefarious was at hand. So by the very act of introducing this concept and this idea, I think the talking point, “Nothing nefarious,” then went across multiple networks, and it became the center of a controversy rather than quelling a controversy."]},{"k":"p","s":["By saying nothing nefarious is at hand, that indeed confirmed something nefarious was at hand, even if the nefariousness was only the mismanagement of the air traffic control systems routers that they claimed caused the problem. By introducing this idea, I believe it did bring to mind that there may be other state actors behind whatever happened, that it could be a cyber attack. It would have been better to say, “We have evidence that this was not a cyber attack but a hardware failure.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["How did the later press conference with Mullin and Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy go from your perspective as an expert on crisis communications?"]},{"k":"p","s":["They handled the questions that they received correctly. They told us as much information as they knew."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, they did seem to downplay the extent of this crisis, because we have to remember the traveling public is not just people trying to get to business meetings."]},{"k":"p","s":["We had football teams stranded. Now ",["football Saturday","https://www.ksnblocal4.com/2026/11/13/sudden-faa-ground-stop-strands-teams-throws-upcoming-sports-weekend-into-chaos/"],", all over the SEC, has been disrupted. And there’s probably disruption in other areas of the country, but to us in the South, ",["SEC football is almost a religious experience on Saturday","https://time.com/5349530/paul-finebaum-football/"],". Luckily, ",["the University of South Carolina football team had already flown out","https://www.thestate.com/sports/college/university-of-south-carolina/usc-womens-basketball/article318071121.html"],". But our marching band was stuck in this crisis, and so we have a lot of ripple effects from something like this happening, and it definitely says to me that this was an emergency situation. It wasn’t simply a crisis, it was an actual emergency of impending disaster-level scale."]},{"k":"p","s":["If it were simply routers being overloaded, as we’ve been told, why wouldn’t they already know this situation and restart those routers the night before or over Friday night after most of the traveling public is out of the air?"]},{"k":"p","s":["What was Mullin’s and Duffy’s job when they got out there? What did they need to do?"]},{"k":"p","s":["To inform the public about the danger, why this happened, the extent of the problem, and what they’re doing to remediate the problem. ",["We keep hearing that they’re asking for US$30 billion","https://www.politico.com/news/2026/11/13/faa-orders-nationwide-grounding-of-passenger-planes-01166043"]," and more to repair the whole infrastructure for the air traffic control system, which is great, but what are they doing right now?"]},{"k":"p","s":["How do we know that flights in the air, right this minute, are any safer than the ones yesterday, a minute before the ground stop? Do we have that information? I don’t feel confident that they addressed that question appropriately. I don’t think that the traveling public entirely feels safe at this point or adequately informed that they will arrive at their destination."]},{"k":"p","s":["They introduced ",["politics into the press conference","https://rollcall.com/factbase/trump/transcript/donald-trump-press-briefing-markwayne-mullin-sean-duffy-faa-ground-stop-november-13-2026/"]," as well, didn’t they?"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s something that they have the prerogative to do. They are ",["both political appointees and members of the cabinet","https://www.c-span.org/event/news-conference/cabinet-officials-brief-on-nationwide-ground-stop/449525"],". So I understand that aspect, but I really wish they had addressed the traveling public’s concerns more overtly before making it political, that they need more money to fix this. We know they need more money to fix it, and I’m sure the American taxpayers are aware of the problem and willing to fund those corrections. But the more expedient issues would be, what about ",["all these people who were stuck in airports","https://www.reuters.com/business/aerospace-defense/thousands-us-flights-canceled-delayed-air-travel-system-recovers-shutdown-2026-11-14/"],"?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Were there warning signs for this crisis?"]},{"k":"p","s":["I believe there were. We had ",["another ground stop about three years ago","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/13/us/2023-ground-stop-faa-pilot-warning-system.html"],", due to air traffic control problems, and that is ",["what we call in crisis communications a “prodrome","https://doi.org/10.4135/9781452275956.n139"],",” a warning sign of larger impending problems. When you see these types of warning signs, it really gives us a reason to think it’s going to get worse."]},{"k":"p","s":["Duffy did say on Nov. 13 that, because of the condition of the air traffic infrastructure, “ ",["you will have more","https://www.kake.com/news/national/you-will-have-more-of-these-unless-system-upgraded-duffy-says-of-outage-that-led/article_4cbc8ca8-cbe2-4119-af1e-6b0de1def505.html"],"” ground stoppages. If you had a piece of advice for the administration regarding their future communications, what would you tell them?"]},{"k":"p","s":["I would say to communicate in advance as much as possible, so if you’re even considering a ground stop, it may be a good idea to put out a public notice so that people don’t go to the airport on a vacation flight, maybe they delay that for a week or two. It might also be a good idea to speak with the airline industry representatives and say, “Here’s what we’re thinking. Can you work with us? How can we make this better for the traveling public?” Also, if 17 of 22 routers were malfunctioning, could we have had a partial ground stop at only the affected airports, rather than a nationwide stop?"]},{"k":"p","s":["My silly last question: Do crisis communications experts have any theories about Friday the 13th?"]},{"k":"p","s":["We consider it more of a superstition, but I have noticed that there does tend to be a lot of activity on Friday the 13th. It might be placebo effect, it might be because we expect something bad to happen and we’re looking for it. But that day does seem to always have some type of activity. This is also when organizations release bad news, oftentimes, they say, “Let’s hold it until Friday the 13th, because bad news is expected.” People will assume, on Friday the 13th, that negative things are going to come out, so the shock value won’t be as much."]}],"chars":6911},"https://theconversation.com/pa-gov-josh-shapiros-popularity-and-get-sh-t-done-attitude-might-not-cut-it-in-crowded-2028-democratic-field-but-he-has-options-295841":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"23d965d241fcf18e18b71bb62ca1e7029d3ca317a43e084d35f86d8cf2c6d57d","read":"https://theconversation.com/pa-gov-josh-shapiros-popularity-and-get-sh-t-done-attitude-might-not-cut-it-in-crowded-2028-democratic-field-but-he-has-options-295841","bytes":183666,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Pa. Gov. Josh Shapiro’s popularity and ‘get sh-t done’ attitude might not cut it in crowded 2028 Democratic field – but he has options","by":[{"n":"Alison Dagnes","r":"Professor of Political & Social Inquiry, Shippensburg University"}],"pub":"2026-11-10T22:21:08Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The ",["2026 midterm elections","https://theconversation.com/topics/2026-midterm-elections-178375"]," swept Democrats into office around the country in such numbers that journalists were running out of synonyms for “ ",["massive","https://www.yahoo.com/news/politics/articles/massive-blue-wave-just-hit-053500218.html"],".”"]},{"k":"p","s":["In Pennsylvania, Gov. Josh Shapiro won reelection by 22 percentage points, ",["winning more than 60% of the vote","https://apnews.com/projects/elections-2026/pennsylvania-governor-results/"]," – something that has been accomplished only ",["twice before in the modern era","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Pennsylvania_gubernatorial_elections"]," in the Keystone State."]},{"k":"p","s":["Not only did Shapiro wipe the floor with his opponent Stacy Garrity, the state treasurer, but he also helped flip four U.S. House seats from red to blue. His coattails ",["benefited down-ballot candidates","https://www.spotlightpa.org/news/2026/09/campaign-finance-pennsylvania-governor-josh-shapiro-stacy-garrity-downballot-elections/"],", helping Democrats solidify their control of the state House and ",["flip the state Senate as well","https://theconversation.com/pennsylvania-democrats-now-have-power-to-push-forward-on-election-reform-marijuana-legalization-and-minimum-wage-increases-295731"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Shapiro’s political stock in Pennsylvania is riding high."]},{"k":"p","s":["I’m a ",["political science professor","https://www.ship.edu/academics/cas/department-of-political-and-social-inquiry/faculty-and-staff-poli-sci/allison-dagnes-bio/"]," and ",["political media researcher","https://scholar.google.com/scholar?hl=en&as_sdt=0%2C39&q=alison+dagnes&btnG="]," in central Pennsylvania, and many of my former students work in Harrisburg. Some are Democrats working for or around the governor; others are Republicans working in different corners of state government. All are finely tuned to the political gossip that swirls around a successful politician whose star is on the rise. It is the worst-kept secret in American politics that Josh Shapiro wants to be president."]},{"k":"p","s":["I’ve met the governor a handful of times and can attest to his George Clooney-level charisma. He’s a hard worker, has maintained a remarkably clean political profile, and is from many accounts a genuinely nice dude."]},{"k":"p","s":["And yet, there are plenty of reasons his ambitions may require some careful timing, regardless of his personal strengths."]},{"k":"h","s":["A reputation for getting stuff done"]},{"k":"p","s":["Shapiro’s political victories didn’t just happen. Over the past four years, he has worked ",["to demonstrate bipartisan competence","https://theconversation.com/gov-josh-shapiro-has-a-reputation-for-getting-things-done-in-pennsylvania-but-not-necessarily-things-all-democrats-like-235854"]," as Pennsylvania’s chief executive, adopting an expression he uses frequently: “ ",["get sh-t done","https://apnews.com/article/josh-shapiro-pennsylvania-swear-word-slogan-45db6d5d09a3a1e39bd13f4af70d1e23"],".”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Now, with Democrats holding the governor’s office and both chambers of the General Assembly, ",["Shapiro told reporters","https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2026/11/04/after-the-flood-01148513"],": “We got the power now, the House, the Senate. We have to deliver.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Shapiro’s ",["approval ratings have remained strong","https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2026/10/30/josh-shapiro-pennsylvania-gubernatorial-race-2028-01137443"],", consistent with his reelection margins. That’s unusual in a state that has swung back and forth between supporting ",["Donald Trump in 2016","https://www.electionreturns.pa.gov/_ENR/General/SummaryResults?ElectionID=54&ElectionType=G&IsActive=0"],", ",["Joe Biden in 2020","https://www.electionreturns.pa.gov/_ENR/General/SummaryResults?ElectionID=83&ElectionType=G&IsActive=0"]," and ",["Trump again in 2024","https://www.electionreturns.pa.gov/General/SummaryResults?ElectionID=105&ElectionType=G&IsActive=0"],", each time by fewer than 2 percentage points."]},{"k":"p","s":["If Shapiro is indeed ",["seriously eyeing the White House","https://thehill.com/homenews/state-watch/5822245-josh-shapiro-2028-speculation-national-action-network/"],", his current popularity will certainly serve him well. But winning the presidency is an enormous undertaking, particularly in a crowded field."]},{"k":"h","s":["Stiff competition in 2028"]},{"k":"p","s":["With Trump unable to run in 2028, the next presidential election will feature open seats for both parties and likely attract many candidates. Democrats, in particular, have a ",["deep bench of attractive potential contenders","https://punchbowl.news/article/campaigns/dems-2028-campaign/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are so many possibilities that Shapiro could find himself running against people very much like him: younger centrists, swing-state politicians and accomplished elected officials with solid records. Consider just a few names that could be part of the conversation: Georgia Sen. Jon Ossoff, Illinois Gov. JB Pritzker and former Chicago Mayor Rahm Emanuel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Shapiro would have to find a way to distinguish himself in a field filled with candidates who can make many of the same arguments about their experience, political appeal and accomplishments. That’s a tall order. A Plan B might be wise."]},{"k":"h","s":["Options beyond the White House"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fortunately for Shapiro, other choices abound."]},{"k":"p","s":["He could run for the Senate in 2028 against incumbent John Fetterman, ",["if Fetterman seeks reelection","https://thehill.com/homenews/6208182-ahmed-moor-challenges-fetterman/"],". This would be a twofer: Shapiro would continue his rise in politics, and he would likely beat a guy he apparently does not like. The two ",["reportedly don’t speak","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/12/us/politics/john-fetterman-josh-shapiro-pennsylvania.html"],", much less get along."]},{"k":"p","s":["Shapiro could also position himself for a vice presidential nomination by attaching himself to another 2028 hopeful. This would buy him time to build his national profile, allow the presidential field to sort itself out and potentially put him in a strong position for another run at the White House down the road. It would also give him an opportunity to demonstrate that he can work effectively on a national stage."]},{"k":"p","s":["Or he could angle for a Cabinet post. The federal government has undergone ",["significant restructuring under DOGE","https://www.city-journal.org/article/doge-spending-cuts-civil-service-elon-musk"]," and Trump’s executive orders. Should a Democrat win the White House in 2028, rebuilding federal agencies and restoring institutional capacity will be a monumental undertaking. Shapiro could be an attractive candidate for a major administrative role."]},{"k":"p","s":["The bottom line for Shapiro is that he will need to distinguish himself from a crowded field of Democrats by emphasizing his statewide victories in a major swing state, impressive fundraising ability and a political voice that ",["can evoke Barack Obama","https://www.tiktok.com/@msnow/video/7421241756592737579?_r=1&refer=player_v1&referer_video_id=7421241756592737579&referrer"]," without alienating either his party or the broader electorate. That’s a tricky feat, even for the most talented politicians."]},{"k":"p","s":["But Nov. 3, 2026, showed us that he knows how to make sh-t happen. Whatever he decides, the next two years will be important for Shapiro, consequential for Democrats, and fascinating for political scientists like me, who will be watching events unfold with a keen eye and, probably, a bucket of popcorn."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more of our stories about ",["Philadelphia and Pennsylvania","https://theconversation.com/us/philadelphia-pennsylvania-news"],", or sign up for our Philadelphia ",["newsletter on Substack","https://tcphilly.substack.com/"],"."]}],"chars":5200},"https://theconversation.com/politics-with-michelle-grattan-allegra-spender-on-community-anger-and-politicians-bad-behaviour-296820":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-18T00:43Z","sha":"b1d51c7ba0f570caad03398f3bed2d8a18d0fbab02cec773805fcc2c80dcc783","read":"https://theconversation.com/politics-with-michelle-grattan-allegra-spender-on-community-anger-and-politicians-bad-behaviour-296820","bytes":177590,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Politics with Michelle Grattan: Allegra Spender on community anger and politicians’ bad behaviour","by":[{"n":"Michelle Grattan","r":"Professorial Fellow, University of Canberra"}],"pub":"2026-11-18T00:22:55Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Independent Allegra Spender is one of the prominent teals who first won at the 2022 election. Along with Zali Steggall, she has now founded a new party called Community Strong Australia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Spender is the member for Wentworth, an affluent inner Sydney seat, once held by Malcolm Turnbull. She has made the economy one of her strong focuses since being elected."]},{"k":"p","s":["As the Senate continues to consider parts of the budget legislation, Spender has been pushing for changing the government’s controversial capital gains tax reform."]},{"k":"p","s":["With her electorate including Bondi, site of last year’s massacre, Spender will have special attention on the royal commission report on antisemitism that will be released next month."]},{"k":"p","s":["Spender joined us on the podcast to talk about these issues and more."]},{"k":"p","s":["On setting up her new party, Spender says it’s been “fun” and she’s attracted interest from all across the country:"]},{"k":"p","s":["It takes a lot of work to set up a political party. It’s not for the faint-hearted. But some of the things that really excite me, we’ve got supporters now from literally 150 electorates around the country, done lots of online events, again, with people from around the country and that’s super exciting to see where the common ground is."]},{"k":"p","s":["A lot of people feel that they don’t have a representation that balances the care of the natural world and the environment, the sort of the social support for us, when people [are] at their most vulnerable. But also an honest approach on how do we grow prosperity in a fair way, but we need to grow the economy and be business focused as well. And so I think that’s been really fun, actually building something that goes beyond just Wentworth, building from the best of the independents’ model, but also something that can go further."]},{"k":"p","s":["On lowering the temperature in politics, Spender says several factors contribute to the current level of community anger:"]},{"k":"p","s":["I think the economy is always a factor in terms of people’s financial stress and personal stress that is driving it. I think behaviour on social media has become normalised to be abusive to others and this is exacerbated by the social media business models effectively to amplify the outrage and also by bots who are contributing."]},{"k":"p","s":["I also think politicians have responsibilities here and I’ve been long a critic of behaviour in the parliament. […] I’ve heard people shout out “rip him another one”, “rip her head off”, calling for people to be stoned in the street. In the parliament. These are people in the chamber where we make the laws for the country are speaking like that and I think it is time for all of us as politicians to look in the mirror and to not just say take the temperature down but take actions in our own behaviours to do so."]},{"k":"p","s":["Spender lays out her proposal (opposed by the government) for overhauling the budget’s capital gain tax changes:"]},{"k":"p","s":["So the government has already passed through the parliament the reform of capital gains tax, where capital gains tax is now going to be indexed against inflation rather than a sort of percentage discount, which has been what we’ve had in place for roughly the last 20 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the government recognised that the indexation model of taxation didn’t really work for particularly for high-growth low-capital businesses and so wanted to do a carve-out for those innovative businesses, because it made the argument that we still need to be a competitive place to start and grow those sorts of businesses."]},{"k":"p","s":["I’m arguing instead, and now with the backing of the four major business groups, the backing of many leading economists like Bob Breunig and Chris Richardson to say, look, give up on the [Innovative Business CGT Concession], replace it with a 40% CGT discount across all businesses and shares. It’s something that would mean [a] top capital gains tax rate of around 28%, which is broadly […] competitive with a lot of other companies. But it’s simple, it’s predictable, it applies to all businesses and I think it would be a better outcome. I’m really urging the government to listen to business on this one."]},{"k":"p","s":["On what she wants to see from the antisemitism royal commission, Spender says:"]},{"k":"p","s":["I think about this in two ways. There’s the security element, which is how do we keep our country safe from terrorists, from people who wish to do harm across the community. And then there’s the cohesion element, which is, how do you create a community and a country that is welcoming to all, where Jewish Australians in particular, but not only Jewish Australians, all Australians, […] feel welcomed. And fully able to participate in civic life across all institutions."]},{"k":"p","s":["How do we develop a new sort of inclusive patriotism where we celebrate Australia’s values, but where those celebrating Australia and its values isn’t about saying, as some people would, “well, I’m more Australian than you are because my family’s been here for longer or because of the colour of my skin or my religion”. Rather than saying, you know, we are here, one nation, people coming together because we’re proud of this country and let’s build on those values which unite us and which give us pride."]}],"chars":5097},"https://theconversation.com/why-sportswomen-are-turning-to-onlyfans-and-what-it-says-about-inequality-in-sport-297131":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-23T18:37Z","sha":"397f4730374a9e5d46afff8e691859ab414595e80cd7cba87c6e68d5eef4b92f","read":"https://theconversation.com/why-sportswomen-are-turning-to-onlyfans-and-what-it-says-about-inequality-in-sport-297131","bytes":185191,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Why sportswomen are turning to OnlyFans – and what it says about inequality in sport","by":[{"n":"Holly Thorpe","r":"Professor in Sociology of Sport and Gender, University of Waikato"},{"n":"Kim Toffoletti","r":"Associate Professor of Sociology, Deakin University"}],"pub":"2026-11-23T17:40:43Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Some of the world’s best athletes ",["are now making more money","https://www.stuff.co.nz/culture/361060345/why-world-champion-athletes-are-becoming-onlyfans-creators"]," on OnlyFans than they do winning championships."]},{"k":"p","s":["From American ultrarunner ",["Camille Herron","https://www.nbcnews.com/sports/olympics/running-pay-bills-only-fans-ultramarathon-camille-herron-sports-rcna607090"]," to Australian motorcycle racer ",["Tayla Relph","https://speedcafe.com/motorcycle-racing-news-2026-tayla-relph-onlyfans-sponsorship-comments-reaction-details-worldwcr/"]," and German Olympic bobsled champion ",["Lisa Buckwitz","https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/german-bobsledder-lisa-buckwitz-reveals-195907631.html"],", a growing number of elite sportswomen are turning to the subscription platform to fund their careers."]},{"k":"p","s":["While some athletes post sexually explicit material, others are using OnlyFans for sponsorship, training footage and behind-the-scenes content."]},{"k":"p","s":["Their growing presence on a site ",["best known for adult content","https://theconversation.com/onlyfans-has-a-split-identity-it-needs-to-declare-its-support-for-adult-content-creators-169358"]," has sparked debate about whether it represents empowerment or exploitation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Sportswomen and the rise of digital media"]},{"k":"p","s":["This trend ",["might be making headlines","https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/nov/19/athletes-onlyfans-earnings"],", but it’s part of a much longer history of sportswomen using their bodies and public profiles to earn money – often in an industry that has undervalued their athletic achievements."]},{"k":"p","s":["In December 1998, Playboy featured German figure skater ",["Katarina Witt","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katarina_Witt"],", a two-time Olympic gold medallist and four-time world champion. The issue ",["reportedly became","https://www.dw.com/en/katarina-witt-the-glitter-and-the-gold/a-18837007"]," only the second in the magazine’s history to sell out worldwide."]},{"k":"p","s":["Other prominent athletes followed, including Olympic swimmer Amanda Beard and professional volleyball player Gabrielle Reece. Sportswomen have also appeared in revealing photo shoots for FHM, Sports Illustrated’s Swimsuit Issue, ESPN The Magazine’s Body Issue and GQ."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 1999, Australia’s national soccer team, the Matildas, appeared in a ",["now infamous nude calendar","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2023-07-30/the-nude-calendar-that-got-the-matildas-in-trouble-with-the-aust/102272414"]," to boost their profile and raise funds."]},{"k":"p","s":["The rise of social media in recent years has now ",["offered sportswomen","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/pdf/10.1080/14413523.2025.2532216"]," new ways to control how they present themselves."]},{"k":"p","s":["Over the past decade, many have used their own accounts to tell their sporting stories, connect with fans, build personal brands and attract sponsors. Doing so has allowed them to bypass mainstream sports media, which ",["has historically marginalised, trivialised and sexualised","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/pdf/10.1177/2167479513476947?casa_token=SGLeQg-jH14AAAAA:thBY-56TU4_PJI1-iJkCeGB0tFYcN9r5IbzxSwvtci66onxn1oud4zCGCOjxyJ8-vfjyuWICr33r"]," women athletes."]},{"k":"p","s":["But this greater control over their public image has also highlighted the pressures sportswomen face to remain visible and commercially appealing."]},{"k":"h","s":["Cultivating ‘desirable athletic femininity’"]},{"k":"p","s":["In research we conducted a decade ago, ",["we analysed","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/pdf/10.1177/0959353517726705?casa_token=SvITmDVu2lkAAAAA:EOrEE5LcmvwUaI7fbo2s95DT5Q3UOapbj4BznZkBg5uar6CD0XyPv8_EeK9cQnHZkV-P2gk4kEMJ"]," the social media accounts of five sportswomen who had some of the largest international followings at the time: tennis stars Serena Williams and Maria Sharapova, motorsport driver Danica Patrick, mixed martial arts fighter Ronda Rousey and professional surfer Alana Blanchard."]},{"k":"p","s":["We found the sportswomen often focused on fashion, friends, family and lifestyle. Many also shared sexualised images emphasising their beauty and femininity to attract attention and build their profiles in a competitive sports media industry."]},{"k":"p","s":["In ",["another study","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/full/10.1177/1469540517747068"],", we examined the considerable labour sportswomen invest in cultivating a marketable, likeable and authentic image of “ ",["desirable athletic femininity","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/abs/10.1177/1469540517747068"],"”."]},{"k":"p","s":["But this online visibility also comes with ",["new risks","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/pdf/10.1080/01490400.2021.1884628?casa_token=aTEECILJoEEAAAAA:I4rB32NGkTtoWke4wOE4m0gtnW6JTS2bKhwKjr15M1avg6KRYnIRrBhQ-Jq95kCXF0XvmQauPLWi"],", including body shaming, trolling and other forms of abuse ",["that can take a toll on sportswomen’s health and wellbeing","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/full/10.1177/21674795251412781"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The use of OnlyFans has divided opinion over sportswomen profiting from their own images. While some see it ",["as a form of economic and bodily empowerment","https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s11199-015-0497-6.pdf"],", others argue that it reinforces existing inequalities in women’s sport."]},{"k":"p","s":["For athletes who choose to share sexualised content, one concern is that it encourages audiences to view sportswomen as sexual objects rather than serious athletes. This could ",["potentially undermine progress","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/pdf/10.1177/2167479512473585?casa_token=2ZQg8Gc-uooAAAAA:nktrVbhJK6R-CEe8APn_LTHbO7Emjnc6KSokbK3-mM_OiDYDXNVsMSjYYz2z2JjhGsRPJvrmieIE"]," towards gender equality in sport."]},{"k":"p","s":["In ",["our previous research","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/pdf/10.1177/0193723517730808?casa_token=wjcwpUS1-FYAAAAA:FGfu-4So0__tY5rvV1oQ3uoiAk44bBfHKrAXuZFg_DO_J_r3fugYd0FacMQyzsD-w1bqCnOmO_dE"],", we examined how different strands of feminism – including ",["third-wave","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Third-wave_feminism"],", ",["postfeminist","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Postfeminism"]," and ",["neoliberal","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/09502386.2013.857361"]," perspectives – interpret sportswomen’s decisions to sexualise their own images. Some emphasise women’s agency and entrepreneurialism, while others see objectification and the reinforcement of inequalities in women’s sport."]},{"k":"p","s":[["The recent backlash","https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/sep/14/sydney-sweeney-advert-global-backlash-what-women-in-sport-look-like"]," from sportswomen against an advertisement featuring actor Sydney Sweeney illustrates these tensions. The ad, which used Sweeney’s sex appeal to promote sports betting, ",["drew criticism","https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/sep/14/ariarne-titmus-comments-sydney-sweeney-sexualising-womens-sport"]," from athletes who argued it reinforced outdated stereotypes about women in sport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Why Sydney Sweeney’s controversial advert goes beyond sexualising women’s sport","https://theconversation.com/why-sydney-sweeneys-controversial-advert-goes-beyond-sexualising-womens-sport-291964"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Such responses suggest a growing resistance to sexualised portrayals, and a desire for sportswomen to be respected and valued for their athletic achievements."]},{"k":"h","s":["Is the gender pay gap driving sportswomen to OnlyFans?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Financial pressures have long influenced athletes’ decisions to sexualise their own images. If sportswomen were paid more fairly, fewer might feel compelled to seek income through platforms such as OnlyFans."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there have been significant improvements in recent years in some sports, ",["the gender pay gap in professional sport","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gender_pay_gap_in_sports"]," remains substantial."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite some notable exceptions, ",["women athletes typically earn considerably less across","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-01-12/abc-elite-athletes-womens-sport-survey-results/106100946"]," several forms of financial compensation. These include salaries, prize money, performance bonuses, sponsorships, endorsements and shares of sporting revenue."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["latest Forbes global rankings","https://www.forbes.com/sites/hanktucker/2026/05/22/why-none-of-2026s-50-highest-paid-athletes-are-women/"]," reveal that for the third consecutive year, not a single woman appeared among the world’s 50 highest-paid athletes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sportswomen are training just as hard as their male counterparts, and they are ",["increasingly filling stadiums","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/14660970.2026.2754042?casa_token=T0Q0lhWbuHwAAAAA%3ARTTNd2zWO4f2WKQ3qb17tR1ELaFPaDT15s6SIQWQ_X3PPNSrPysEa6Fbh2LTZKApE_GUlR586-me"]," and ",["attracting growing audiences","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/full/10.1177/21674795251368994?casa_token=ScfF-0gxC2MAAAAA%3Awox-2a5ndpvQVjLTQhWajBbFJKhJZc-TS4DJ2dkpmem5IYwLbCGiNPfph-rGPsYOc_Cryybb4E_W"],". Yet the gendered economy of sport means that many sportswomen are not earning enough to focus full-time on training and competing."]},{"k":"p","s":["OnlyFans may seem like an extreme way to fund a sporting career, but rather than blaming sportswomen, we should acknowledge the inequalities that make it so difficult for many to pursue their sporting ambitions."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the same time, we need to consider the risks such platforms may pose to individual athletes and the wider women’s sport movement."]}],"chars":5773},"https://theconversation.com/a-bigger-parliament-would-fix-the-overhang-problem-the-case-for-more-mps-297034":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-25T18:52Z","sha":"8b81caf4fab45033d620967c56315eecca802af85f83784522c158530c7eb0db","read":"https://theconversation.com/a-bigger-parliament-would-fix-the-overhang-problem-the-case-for-more-mps-297034","bytes":178391,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"A bigger parliament would fix the overhang problem: the case for more MPs","by":[{"n":"Brian S. Roper","r":"Associate Professor of Politics, University of Otago"}],"pub":"2026-11-25T18:03:57Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["In all the debate about the problems with the MMP system thrown up by an ",["unprecedented election result","https://theconversation.com/nzs-next-government-hangs-in-the-balance-2026-election-results-at-a-glance-295556"],", there has been remarkably little discussion of the main factor threatening the proportionality of parliament."]},{"k":"p","s":["That is the historically and comparatively small size of New Zealand’s parliament. In fact, historical statistics show parliament is now the smallest it has ever been relative to the total population."]},{"k":"p","s":["Combined with other factors – strategic vote splitting and mismatched numbers of electorate and party-list seats – this has created the conditions for an unusually ",["large overhang","https://theconversation.com/what-really-drove-nzs-election-overhang-and-what-can-be-done-about-it-296144"]," of parliamentary seats and a disproportionate outcome."]},{"k":"p","s":["With final election results due on Friday, attention will inevitably focus on which parties might be able to form a coalition government."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the overhang question will not go away, and any subsequent review of MMP must look at the logic of increasing the size of parliament."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why is parliament so small?"]},{"k":"p","s":["When the first Labour government was elected in 1935, there were 80 MPs for a population of 1.56 million, a ratio of one MP per 19,527 people."]},{"k":"p","s":["Parliament had 80 MPs until 1966, by which time the population had increased to 2.7 million, a ratio of one MP per 33,461 people."]},{"k":"p","s":["The 1965 ",["Electoral Amendment Act","https://www.legislation.govt.nz/act/public/1965/17/en/latest/#"]," allowed the size of parliament to increase relative to North Island population growth. The number of MPs increased from 84 in 1969 to 99 in 1993."]},{"k":"p","s":["Parliament increased to 120 MPs with the ",["first MMP election","https://elections.nz/democracy-in-nz/what-is-new-zealands-system-of-government/what-is-mmp/the-introduction-of-mmp"]," in 1996 when the population was 3.6 million: one MP per 30,153 people."]},{"k":"p","s":["Since then, parliamentary seats have remained fixed at 120 while the population has increased to 5,372,400 – an historically high ratio of one MP per 44,770 people."]},{"k":"p","s":["The problem becomes even clearer when we compare the New Zealand parliament to those of other small countries with market economies, liberal democracies and broadly similar population sizes."]},{"k":"p","s":["For example, ",["Finland","https://data.ipu.org/parliament/FI/FI-LC01/"]," (population 5.7 million) has 200 MPs. ",["Ireland","https://data.ipu.org/parliament/IE/IE-LC01/"]," (5.5 million) has a lower house consisting of 174 members. ",["Norway","https://data.ipu.org/parliament/NO/NO-LC01/"]," (5.7 million) has 169 MPs, and ",["Denmark","https://data.ipu.org/parliament/DK/DK-LC01/"]," (6.03 million) 179 MPs."]},{"k":"p","s":["One factor contributing to the size of the current parliamentary overhang is that, since 1996, the number of electorate MPs has been adjusted upwards to match a rising population while the overall size of parliament has not."]},{"k":"p","s":["Parliament ignored the 1986 ",["Royal Commission on the Electoral System","https://elections.nz/democracy-in-nz/what-is-new-zealands-system-of-government/report-of-the-royal-commission-on-the-electoral-system"]," recommendation of maintaining a balance of 60 electorate seats and 60 list seats."]},{"k":"p","s":["Instead, it set the number of electorate seats at 65 for the 1996 election, or 54% of the total seats at that time. This has since increased to 71 seats, in turn increasing the percentage of electorate seats in parliament."]},{"k":"p","s":["Once the final result of the 2026 election is determined, electorate seats are likely to make up around 62% of a parliament enlarged by between nine and 11 overhang seats."]},{"k":"h","s":["Larger parliaments are here to stay"]},{"k":"p","s":["MMP cannot ensure the proportionality of party representation with such a high ratio of electorate seats to list seats."]},{"k":"p","s":["One solution would be to reduce the number of electorate seats. But this is unlikely to be supported by Te Pāti Māori or the centre-right parties, for whom electorate seats have become crucial."]},{"k":"p","s":["A simpler solution would be to adjust the overall size of parliament. For example, an increase to 171 seats would generate a ratio of one MP to 31,418 people, only slightly higher than in 1996."]},{"k":"p","s":["Assuming there were no overhangs, this would reduce the electorate seats to 41.5% of the total seats in parliament."]},{"k":"p","s":["Improving the proportionality of party representation would also enhance the legitimacy of the electoral system, diminish the ",["current dominance of the executive branch","https://theconversation.com/nz-governments-enjoy-an-executive-paradise-a-longer-parliamentary-term-wont-change-that-251139"]," of government, and enhance the gender and ethnic representativeness of parliament."]},{"k":"p","s":["In any case, the days of a 120-seat parliament are over. If no formal changes are made to the MMP system, future parliaments will continue to be substantially larger."]},{"k":"p","s":["Parties will logically adapt to the new reality. For example, Labour and the Greens might respond to National’s hold over the electorate seats by reaching an agreement with Te Pāti Māori to split party and electorate votes."]},{"k":"p","s":["This vote splitting strategy would likely create at least a six-seat overhang on the left. That could be augmented by Labour and the Greens adopting a shared strategy of encouraging voters to split their electorate and party votes in marginal electorates."]},{"k":"h","s":["It’s the size, not the system"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are ",["other aspects of the MMP system","https://theconversation.com/the-election-was-an-mmp-special-nows-the-time-to-tune-the-system-not-scapegoat-it-296909"]," that could be changed, too. New Zealand could follow the German example and simply eliminate overhang seats. The 5% threshold for party representation could be reduced, and electorate seats set at less than 50%."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the past, New Zealanders have displayed a preference for a smaller parliament. The ",["citizens initiated referendum in 1999","https://elections.nz/democracy-in-nz/historical-events/1995-2013-referendums"],", which asked whether the House of Representatives should be reduced from 120 members to 99, saw 81.5% in favour of reducing the size of parliament."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the outcome was largely due to widespread distrust of politicians resulting from the ",["rapid implementation of unpopular neoliberal policies","https://theconversation.com/a-nation-reinvented-40-years-on-from-its-1984-victory-the-fourth-labour-government-still-defines-nz-232133"]," from 1984 to 1999. There would likely be more support for increasing the size of parliament now the disadvantages of a small one are becoming clearer."]},{"k":"p","s":["Overall, political parties on the right tend to favour limiting or reducing the size of parliament, in keeping with their preference for smaller government. Parties on the left have (so far) displayed little appetite for increasing its size."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ultimately, however, the issue will have to be addressed."]},{"k":"p","s":["The problem of disproportionality caused by a large number of overhang seats – itself the result of strategic vote splitting and population increase over time – is largely due to the small size of parliament, not the electoral system itself."]}],"chars":5776}};
